  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+3)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\u27e8\\frac{1}{1+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=1$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
